sparky-stereo-camera 0.1.3 (2026-11-26)
  * Only settings are saved (ORDER 678): a control is kept only when it has a range (or is a menu or a boolean), is not read-only, write-only, volatile, a relative or speed control (a movement) or an action, and is active when it is read; every V4L2 control flag has its rule (README).
  * The apply step sets the controls that change the picture's layout, then the mode, then the other controls in passes with fresh flags, so a governing control (automatic white balance, exposure, focus) goes before the value it governs, whatever its id; a saved setting still inactive at the end keeps its value and no problem.
  * An entry written by 0.1.0 to 0.1.2 is cleaned once when its camera is present (the iMac's White Balance Temperature and Iris, Relative), each removal in the journal, and the problems kept for those entries are cleared; the entry is marked version=2.
  * A camera with no saved mode starts at its largest picture and, at that size, its highest frame rate (ORDER 682): at plug-in, on the page's first values and with Defaults; a known machine's table entry can name the formats that camera delivers correctly. The page saves a mode only when the person chose one.
  * A control's default outside its own range (the A10's sharpness, 120 for 0 to 100) is taken as the driver holds it, so a reset no longer saves it.
  * The page says why a control is not kept (moves the camera, changes by itself, no range, held by another program), follows a governing control at once, and keeps a refused mode or reset on screen; five packing names missing since 0.1.2 now come translated from the stereo layer's catalogues.
  * The user service knows a camera plugged in again by PipeWire's object.serial, which is never given twice: a camera unplugged and plugged in again within one pass got its old node id back and was not applied.

sparky-stereo-camera 0.1.1 (2026-11-20)
  * Translate the System Settings search keywords (ORDER 46).

sparky-stereo-camera 0.1.0 (2026-11-15)
  * First release (ORDER 570): the Camera page of System Settings, under Multimedia beside Sound.
  * The default camera is WirePlumber's default.configured.video.source; format, size and frame rate and the camera's own controls are set on the V4L2 device and kept in ~/.config/sparky-stereo-camera/cameras.ini; a user service applies them again when a camera is plugged in.
  * A live preview from PipeWire; a two-lens camera is given its packing (the stereo layer's list) and its pair is shown as a declared full side by side picture.
  * Every refusal, a held camera, no camera and a failed preview are said on the page; ten languages.
